 a card and we still have control.\n\nReason:\nPlaying ♠5 is the optimal move because:\n1. It\'s a free play, so I set the tempo\n2. My teammate has 1 card and needs to play it to win\n3. A low single gives teammate the maximum opportunity to beat it (any card 6 or higher works)\n4. Even if landlord plays, they waste a card, and I still have strong cards (A, K, triple 6s) to control subsequent plays\n5. This is a cooperative strategy - helping my teammate win is just as good as winning myself\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠5"]}'}
